diff --git a/RESOURCE-INTEGRATION.md b/RESOURCE-INTEGRATION.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e1eaff3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/RESOURCE-INTEGRATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,132 @@
+# Native user-client staging integration, default off
+
+The isolated branch wires the parser into the actual `NativeAdrenoUserClient`
+body and `AGXDeviceUserClient` wrapper. This is source-only, validation-only
+integration. `NATIVE_ADRENO_EXPERIMENTAL_RESOURCE_STAGING` defaults to zero.
+No board/root feed, selected profile, running kernel or published AIR probe is
+changed. Native execution capabilities remain unavailable.
+
+## Lock and identity audit
+
+The wrapper's shared `g.lock` serializes core dispatch, map/free, token lookup
+and close. Existing fence waits release/reacquire it for each zero-timeout poll.
+Each core owns its Entry array and client handles; the shared VM's mapping handle
+is not the client handle. VM `describe()` provides live mapped size, IOVA and
+actual permissions and fails on partial/poisoned mappings. All staging lookup
+and teardown run under the same namespace lock.
+
+With the staging source opt-in, kernel atomic monotonic identities name core
+owners, backing Entry incarnations, mapping generations and Session incarnations.
+They saturate rather than wrap. They are never seeded by packet owner fields,
+PID, fd, pointers or a guessed generation. Recreating a Session on an open core
+gets a fresh incarnation: a partially successful close cannot resurrect old
+tokens. Freeing/replacing a BO changes backing/map identities.
+
+Resource lookup checks this core's own Entry, mapped/liveness/quarantine state,
+real VM IOVA/extent and `memory.bytes()`, then uses actual VM permissions. Backing
+cookies currently identify allocation objects for **validation**. Distinct imports
+that alias physical pages still need canonicalization before any scoped-cache
+capability can become available.
+
+## Exact experimental receivers
+
+Only with the source opt-in, both core size dispatch and the wrapper's direct/
+tunneled paths admit these experimental methods:
+
+| Method | Input/output | Behavior |
+|---|---|---|
+| `0x52540001` staging | 408 / 32 bytes | Owner-scoped Begin/pages/Seal/Abort through the actual core |
+| `0x52540002` mapping | 8 / 40 bytes | Client handle in; handle, real generation, IOVA, full extent, permissions and reserved=0 out |
+
+Default-off core dispatch rejects both methods without allocation or modifying
+output. Legacy query/version/flags remain unchanged, and no execution readiness
+is advertised even with the staging source flag. Direct requests reject scalar
+arguments and wrong fixed sizes. The tunnel's existing header removal reaches
+the same exact core validator under `g.lock`.
+
+The generation query addresses a real producer gap: ABI-v1 BoAlloc/BoMap replies
+and the published bridge's BO records have no generation. Future producer wiring
+must issue this exact mapping query (or another reviewed versioned reply) after
+mapping, then carry its actual generation into every BO/IB record. The published
+bridge is unchanged and is not yet connected to this receiver. Never supply 1
+or accept an owner/generation solely because the caller asserted it.
+
+Core Session storage uses actual `IOMalloc`/`IOFree` adapters. Base driver core
+capacity is its real `NativeAdrenoClientMaxObjects` (1024), even though the generic
+transport supports 4096; no unrelated board capacity patch is silently applied.
+
+The core uses `Session::createValidationOnly()` with real lookup. Private Job
+creation uses the immutable validator, but Session refuses `submitSealed()` before
+any Job hook. Every execution hook independently refuses too. No dispatch/opcode
+exposes Job submission. Thus internal validator flags cannot enable GPU execution.
+Execution readiness still requires real queue/context, mapping-pin, cache and
+completion hooks plus capability negotiation.
+
+## Teardown and OS references
+
+Core close/releaseAll first closes staging; Busy stops BO unmap/release. The
+wrapper's actual class has a retirement flag and a bounded registry (three user
+slots plus the kernel slot) that takes an OSObject `retain()` on deferred close.
+The existing kernel poller services that registry under `g.lock`, then terminates/
+`release()`s only after Session and ordinary client teardown succeed. Failed
+retirement keeps core, Session, callback context, VM and slot alive; no force free.
+Polling uses zero-timeout ordinary teardown and never treats a timeout/prefix
+fence as quiescence. Source flag off preserves the prior ordinary close path.
+
+Validation-only staging cannot create in-flight jobs, so native deferred GPU
+retirement is not exercised by this integration yet. The registry/adapters are
+source wiring, not proof of actual OSObject or GPU retirement on hardware.
+
+## Verification and remaining gates
+
+```sh
+python3 tests/run-resource-client.py
+bash tests/run-resource-transactions.sh
+bash tests/run-resources.sh
+python3 tests/compile-resource-client-arm64.py --output /tmp/resource-client-arm64
+```
+
+The actual core/VM/memory/ring bodies pass ASan/UBSan with staging off and on over
+software SMMU/CP peers. Tests cover unmapped/freed/other-client generation query,
+actual read-only VM permission refusal at Seal, allocation cleanup, fresh Session
+identity after partial teardown, unchanged ABI flags and no staging CP writes,
+cache calls or outstanding jobs. Staging metadata returns to its exact baseline.
+Legacy software table roots are intentionally retained, so this existing fixture
+uses leak detection off; new metadata lifetime is checked explicitly. Separate
+49 transaction/33 Job sanitizer cases retain ordinary leak checks. ARM `dsb sy`
+remains unchanged; x86 host peers use a CPU fence instead of invalid ARM assembly.
+
+Six plain ARMv8-A Mach-O objects compile (core/Job/transaction, source flag off/on).
+The check uses authored declarations for IOKit symbols and allocation macros;
+it is **not an XNU SDK build**, linking or runtime ABI evidence. No local Xcode SDK
+was available. `NativeAdrenoPublish.cpp` was not SDK-compiled. Full native SDK/
+kernel-header compilation of the wrapper is a required gate before selecting it.
+
+The separate internal [resource queue](RESOURCE-QUEUE.md) now wires actual VM
+mapping pins, whole-used-BO maintenance and Ring/CP-fence retirement for an initial
+single-in-flight owned-BO path. The wire receiver remains validation-only: it does
+not expose this queue or establish CPU exclusion, imported aliases, actual reset,
+capability negotiation or safe native context ownership. Those and hardware
+qualification remain open; execution readiness and profile selection stay off.
+
+### Native header compile gate
+
+`tests/compile-resource-client-xnu.py` consumes the **actual**
+`IOPlatformExpert.cpo.json` left by the matching XNU build, preserving its target,
+configuration includes, generated headers and working directory. It compiles
+`NativeAdrenoPublish`, core, VM, immutable Job and transaction units with staging
+both off and on; the current gate also includes actual memory and the new resource
+queue for fourteen plain ARM64 Mach-O objects. `-H` traces and SHA-256 binds
+actual IOLib/IOUserClient/OSObject/IOMemoryDescriptor headers to explicitly declared
+real source/SDK roots; a declaration-only substitute outside those roots fails.
+It records each exact command, source/object hashes, failures and header hashes.
+It does not modify or select the board's provider archive. It still does not prove
+final linking, hardware behavior or safe enabling. The script's local helper
+checks are not a completed SDK gate; run it on the original macOS kernel builder.
+
+```sh
+python3 tests/compile-resource-client-xnu.py \
+  --record "$UNIXNU/build/xnu-12377.121.6/ios-obj/DEVELOPMENT_ARM64_BCM2837/iokit/DEVELOPMENT/IOPlatformExpert.cpo.json" \
+  --unixnu "$UNIXNU" --header-root "$UNIXNU" \
+  --output /tmp/resource-xnu-objects
+```
