@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# Experimental complete-resource job boundary
+
+Base: `805c7e4bfb7451eb6923f4a14dea8c657b9be7d2`, the exact driver gitlink in
+the board's root checkout (`work/ios27-port/unixnu`, root commit
+`107af906532d252ef6ba7aff0c43f11e571d3fa1`) and the local control root
+(`UniXNU`, root commit `68c513467bb6c44106c053c410582c1d14f96dd7`). Board/root
+feeds and the board lock contain no driver override. The worktree is isolated;
+no root gitlink, board profile, image, published ABI or existing submit body changes.
+
+`NativeAdrenoResources.{h,cpp}` supplies a portable production-body validator and
+explicit job owner. It copies a complete referenced-resource list and separate
+IBs into privately owned storage, validates live client handles/generations,
+mapping permissions and overflow-safe ranges, merges duplicate uses and backing
+cache intervals, and retains distinct GPU mappings. IBs need declared read/execute
+access and must lie within the declared resource range. Non-IB resources remain
+in both residency and cache manifests. This contract does not discover hidden PM4
+addresses or establish command isolation.
+
+The callback integration must provide real native mappings, atomic revalidated
+holds, scoped cache operations, queue ownership and actual fence/quiescence
+observation. Hold failures release only references successfully held before GPU
+submit. Publication/enqueue happen only after every resource and IB validates
+and every unique mapping is held. `enqueue` receives immutable uses and commands
+plus the exact owner/queue. It must revalidate queue ownership/liveness and retain
+the queue/context until its work finishes.
+
+`Accepted` means the returned fence covers **all** accepted work, including known
+partial submission failures. `Uncertain` may have an unknown tail: even completing
+a known prefix fence cannot release those pins. Timeout/device-lost/uncertain
+completion keeps storage and resources. `destroy()` returns Busy without freeing
+them. Only real completion plus successful CPU acquisition, or proven GPU
+cancel/quiescence plus acquisition, retires pins. Callers must retain Busy jobs
+and arrange observation or recovery; process/client exit cannot free them blindly.
+Prepared/rejected jobs can be destroyed without GPU completion.
+
+Callbacks, allocation and object ownership must outlive the job, be externally
+serialized, non-reentrant and non-throwing. Allocators provide max_align_t-aligned
+memory. Lookup/holds and client namespace mutation must share serialization;
+holds revalidate the whole mapping incarnation atomically. Cache callbacks get
+canonical backing spans and access bits; acquisition should select GPU-written
+spans. Backing identity/offset must represent physical aliasing correctly.
+
+The capability structure is an **internal contract, not a wire extension**.
+All of complete resources, retention through fence and scoped cache semantics
+must be explicitly available. ABI v1 does not imply any of them; an absent/old
+capability is rejected before allocation, lookup, cache or submission. No existing
+kernel advertises this interface and no transport/profile is selected here.
+
+Actual API constraints checked before choosing transport: current
+`NativeAdrenoAbiSubmit` is 416 bytes with 16 IBs, and both the direct IOKit dispatch
+and core request validator require exact fixed-size records. The AGX tunnel strips
+8 bytes then uses the same core validator. There is no established 4096-BO wire
+message. A bounded [transaction implementation](RESOURCE-TRANSACTION.md) now
+provides paged upload/seal/abort and immutable Job creation. Native IOKit dispatch,
+capability publication and VM/cache hooks remain unintegrated; there is no
+silent legacy/global-cache fallback.
+
+Run the exact implementation bodies under ASan/UBSan without exceptions or RTTI:
+
+```sh
+bash tests/run-resources.sh
+```
+
+33 host cases cover immutable full manifests, non-IB retention, bounds/permissions/
+ownership, all allocator/hold failures, stale lookup-to-hold changes, duplicate
+uses, overlapping/transitive backing aliases, partial acceptance and unknown
+prefix fences, timeouts, acquisition failure and proven-quiescence recovery.
+The separate experimental renderer's MSM adapter suite adds 25 cases, including
+all 4096 full BOs and strict old-capability refusal. These are host callback/fault
+tests; native IOKit transport, cache maintenance and physical GPU lifetime behavior
+are still unproven for this new boundary.
