index 0000000..2d8ff8b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/RESOURCE-QUEUE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# Native complete-resource queue, source-only and unselected
+
+`NativeAdrenoResourceQueue` now connects the immutable resource Job to actual
+`NativeAdrenoUserClient` descriptions, `NativeAdrenoVm` pin/cache methods and
+`NativeAdrenoRing` PM4/fence code. This is executable driver source exercised over
+host SMMU/CP peers. It is not a new wire method, negotiated capability or enabled
+system renderer. The staging receiver remains validation-only and default-off.
+
+The first path deliberately admits one Job on an idle ring. Admission authenticates
+its kernel-bound owner/queue before pins or cache operations, rejects poison and
+fence-counter exhaustion, and never falls back to legacy `NativeAdrenoSubmit`.
+The Job holds every used BO, including non-IB textures/shader/descriptors. Holds
+revalidate exact client generation, backing/mapping incarnation, real IOVA, extent
+and permission against the actual VM before incrementing mapping+memory references.
+
+Scoped maintenance covers only complete **used** BOs. CPU clean/invalidate occurs
+before GPU access regardless of write-combine or speculative coherency flags.
+After an actual CP timestamp completion, only declared GPU-written BOs are
+invalidated; this path never writes CPU dirt back over GPU results. Inactive
+resident BOs are not scanned. Four saturating VM counters record successful object
+and byte counts. There is no dirty epoch/precise range/barrier batching claim yet.
+
+The enqueue path independently revalidates resources and command coverage, emits
+up to128 complete IB packets into one framed ring commit, and invalidates the
+actual context TLB. A poisoned/uncertain commit retains every resource. No prefix
+fence, timeout, task exit or missing watchdog proves quiescence; recovery currently
+returns false until a real reset/cancel implementation exists.
+
+Pin retirement is now failure-aware. A failed native release retains that pin and
+all remaining pins plus Job storage; subsequent poll/recover retries only the
+unreleased pins. Successful pins are never dropped twice. Completed CPU acquire
+and proven quiescence are not repeated merely because a release failed. A closed
+Session remains pollable by its retained retirement owner until destroy succeeds.
+
+The initial kernel backing callback refuses all imports: distinct imported
+IOSurface mappings still need canonical physical aliases and CPU/GPU ownership.
+The caller must hold the namespace/queue gate, maintain exclusive CPU access and
+retain the queue, callback context, VM and Ring until every Job is destroyed.
+Those are trusted kernel caller preconditions, not enforcement established by
+constructing this class. Enabling arbitrary app submissions requires real CPU
+PREP/FINI or equivalent ownership, imported-plane/layout validation, fences and
+native connection/capability negotiation. The current user-client does not expose
+this execution path, and it does not own a queue context for in-flight Sessions.
+
+## Meaningful source tests
+
+`tests/run-resource-client.py` runs actual core, VM, memory, Ring and new queue
+bodies under ASan/UBSan with staging off/on over software SMMU/CP peers. A Job with
+three used4KiB BOs plus one inactive BO publishes12KiB, acquires4KiB, holds the
+non-IB resources through a delayed CP fence, refuses free while in flight and
+performs no legacy/global submit. Wrong queue and competing in-flight admission
+produce no pins/cache/CP side effects. Acquisition failure retains all references
+for retry; partial publication failure cannot enqueue; stale namespace detection
+rolls back earlier holds without cache work. Host physical cache callbacks record
+the invalidate operation; they do not emulate actual CPU cache coherency.
+
+Separate39 Job cases cover partial release failures after completion, pre-submit
+rollback, quiesced recovery and admission. The50 Session cases prove failed native
+retirement keeps a closed Session alive and pollable. The25 MSM adapter tests still
+pass. Existing software SMMU fixture roots intentionally remain mounted, so that
+core fixture uses leak detection off; Job and Session suites keep ordinary leak
+checks. Actual XNU SDK object compilation, final native linking and hardware queue
+behavior remain separate required gates. No 60/90Hz, wallpaper or compositor
+performance follows from host success.
diff --git a/RESOURCE-TRANSACTION.md b/RESOURCE-TRANSACTION.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a9f9c97
--- /dev/null
+++ b/RESOURCE-TRANSACTION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@
+# Bounded resource transaction protocol, experimental
+
+`NativeAdrenoResourceTransaction.{h,cpp}` implements the exact parser, owner-scoped
+staging storage, token/sequence state and seal-to-`Job` validation. The follow-on
+[core integration](RESOURCE-INTEGRATION.md) reserves default-off experimental
+selectors; no published capability or selected profile enables it.
+Host tests exercise the implementation bodies; native IOKit transport and real
+VM/cache hooks are still unproven for this path.
+
+## Fixed inline sizes and capability boundary
+
+Requests are **408 bytes**, leaving 8 bytes for the AGX tunnel within a 416-byte
+total. Replies are **32 bytes**. Future direct dispatch must check exactly 408/32;
+tunnel dispatch must check 416/32 before removing its header. Existing ABI-v1
+Submit expects a different 416-byte record and must reject these packets. Fitting
+the size envelope does not make the current dispatch accept this format.
+There are no pointers or out-of-line arrays.
+
+`schema()` describes format facts in 32 bytes: magic, version, request/reply sizes,
+max resources/IBs, required Job flags, reserved. Required flags are complete
+resources, retention through completion and scoped cache. Requirements are not
+available runtime capabilities. Session creation rejects missing/old internal
+capabilities before allocation.
+
+Future negotiation needs a separately assigned exact-size query that distinguishes
+available semantics from schema requirements. Old kernels must return unsupported;
+clients must refuse the path. Do not infer readiness from ABI-v1 or a protocol
+number. Advertise only after native VM/cache/pins, queue ownership and close-time
+retirement are integrated and validated. No query/method IDs are assigned here
+and there is no legacy/global-cache fallback. The follow-on integration's mapping
+generation query is separate from execution-capability negotiation.
+
+## Layout and operations
+
+All fields are little endian; static assertions fix sizes. The parser first copies
+the complete request, safely handling unaligned caller storage.
+
+| Request offset | Field |
+|---:|---|
+| 0 / 4 / 8 / 12 | u32 magic `0x31524d4e`, version 1, operation, flags=0 |
+| 16 / 24 | u64 token ID, generation |
+| 32 / 36 | u32 sequence, page record count |
+| 40 / 44 | u32 declared resource/IB totals |
+| 48 / 52 | u32 exact payload bytes, reserved=0 |
+| 56 | 352 inline payload bytes; unused bytes zero |
+
+Reply offsets: u32 status/state at 0/4, u64 token/generation at 8/16, u32 next
+sequence/internal Error at 24/28. Unauthorized calls reveal no token/generation/
+sequence. Authentication comes from the native connection, never packet fields.
+Internal Error does not imply GPU execution or fault absence.
+
+| Operation | Requirement and effect |
+|---|---|
+| Begin=1 | Zero token/generation/sequence/count; totals within 1..4096 BOs and 1..128 IBs; exactly 8 payload bytes for queue; allocate arrays and return token/sequence 1 |
+| Resources=2 | Up to 8×40-byte full-BO Resource records; exact bytes/count, resource phase only |
+| Ibs=3 | Up to 11×32-byte IB records; resource total must already be complete |
+| Seal=4 | Zero count/payload; both totals complete; validate full live extents, create immutable Job, release upload arrays |
+| Abort=5 | Zero count/payload; discard incomplete upload or safe prepared/completed/rejected Job; unresolved work returns Busy |
+
+Every non-Begin packet needs the exact active token/generation, totals and next
+sequence. Successful pages and Seal advance once. Replay, gaps, wrong phase,
+excess/empty pages, truncated/oversized packets, nonzero padding, unknown flags
+and wrong totals cannot advance state. A page validates fully before copying
+records. Resources contain handle/generation, offset=0, full bytes, access and
+reserved=0; IBs contain handle/generation/offset/bytes. Seal and the Job's atomic
+hold contract validate permissions, ownership, liveness and containment before
+GPU effects.
+
+One transaction can be staged/sealed per Session. Begin while occupied returns
+Busy without eviction. Begin after abort gets a new generation. Replayed Begin
+in an idle session creates a fresh transaction; old pages remain stale. Begin
+allocation failure consumes a generation, frees partial storage and issues no
+token. Generation never wraps. Seal allocation failure retains the upload for
+retry at the same sequence. Invalid immutable data requires Abort to replace it.
+
+## Identity, bounds and close
+
+Token ID is a nonzero kernel-issued connection incarnation, never reused for that
+owner across close/reconnect and never derived from an fd, PID or user pointer.
+Generation increases within the connection. Every request checks authenticated
+owner before reading bytes. The eventual native owner/incarnation provider must
+enforce those guarantees; tokens are not secrets and arbitrary user-supplied owner
+arguments are not authentication.
+
+At 4096 BOs/128 IBs, upload plus copied Job allocation peak is tested below 1 MiB,
+excluding allocator metadata/existing GPU BOs. Pages allocate nothing. Native
+connection management must also enforce connection/global quotas.
+
+Seal uses read-only lookup and immutable validation: no holds, cache or enqueue.
+`submitSealed()` is a future internal integration entry, deliberately absent from
+wire operations. Exact owner/queue and complete resources reach Job enqueue;
+replay cannot submit the same Job twice.
+
+Close forbids further packets and frees incomplete/prepared state. In-flight or
+uncertain jobs make close/destroy return Busy with storage/pins intact. A retirement
+owner must retain Session, context/VM, callback context and allocator after client
+close, then poll or recover through proven quiescence. A known prefix fence does
+not cover an unknown tail. Covering completion or proven cancel/quiescence, plus
+CPU acquisition, is required before release. Actual native client teardown is
+not wired to this owner yet and must never free Busy state blindly.
+
+## Host gate
+
+```sh
+bash tests/run-resource-transactions.sh
+bash tests/run-resources.sh
+```
+
+49 transaction and 33 Job cases pass ASan/UBSan with exceptions/RTTI disabled.
+Tests include 4096/128 maxima, replay/sequence/phase, every allocation failure,
+lengths/padding, full BO extents, wrong owner/cross-connection/old generation,
+abort/retry, seal without GPU effects, client close in each phase and unknown-tail
+quiescence. This proves host parser/state/lifetime behavior only.
